# What never reaches the image's build context.
#
# THIS FILE IS A SECRET BOUNDARY BEFORE IT IS AN OPTIMISATION. `apps/web/.env`
# is gitignored, so it is invisible in a diff and present on every developer's
# machine, and a `COPY . .` puts it in a layer of a PUBLIC image. ADR-0114 is
# the record that a published string cannot be taken back.
#
# `packages/config/src/image.test.ts` fails if one of the four load-bearing
# patterns goes missing or is re-included below.

# The credentials. Every form: `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production`.
**/.env*

# The host's modules. Wrong platform's binaries, and the image installs its own.
**/node_modules

# A stale build, which would shadow the one this image makes.
**/.next
**/.turbo

# The history. Large, and nothing in the build reads it.
.git
.gitignore
.gitleaksignore

# Test and tooling output.
**/coverage
**/.vitest
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Nothing in the build reads these, and excluding them means editing a record
# or a workflow does not invalidate the install layer.
docs
.github
.claude
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
README.md

# LICENSE is deliberately NOT here. The image is a conveyance of the work, and
# AGPL-3.0 section 4 asks that a copy of the licence go with it; the runner
# stage copies it to /app/LICENSE. The `licenses` label names the election, and
# the text is what the election is an election OF.

# Editor and operating system leavings.
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
